   "text": "✗ **k11i_paper_only_elimination_and_bundle20001_single_domino_c6_trap** · hypothesis\n\nThe analytical chain Theorems 1-30 eliminates Class 6 purely on paper without finite GPU tree search, and scheduling we_star_saddle_free_remaining_gpu.json purely by orbit count (51-orbit Bundle 20001 first on Shard 0) avoids GPU batch stalls.\n\n*why dead:* [L-C9G-033=0] [obstruction=compute_wall] Falsified on both clauses: (1) on Seed Orbits 0 and 1670 (h=0, C_12), while Theorems 1-30 compress the tree >10^12x and force sols=0 at d12, Seed Orbit 0 still has 113,567 d8 branches (19.34B d6 nodes) and Seed Orbit 1670 has 90,674 d8 branches before hitting the d10/d12 wall; (2) Bundle 20001 (51 orbits, c6=[0,2,1,6,5,9]) has only 1 full domino in c6 (n_doms_in_c6=1) and r6=42, stalling Shard 0 on batch 1 for >35m vs 45-210s/batch when n_doms_in_c6 >= 2.",
